156
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,900
Yes, this time when I went to perform at KCON in LA...

157
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,700
It's usually in things like pho.

158
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:34,610
But this time, it came on top of a pizza.

159
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:36,490
Still, wouldn't it be good?

160
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:38,916
Because Mexican food naturally has a lot...

161
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,810
Right, right, like Mexican pizza and stuff.

162
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,086
Mexican food uses a lot of it.

163
00:05:42,110 --> 00:05:44,449
Yes, so I picked it all off like this.

164
00:05:44,450 --> 00:05:45,450
Did you?

165
00:05:45,451 --> 00:05:47,126
If you do that, BamBam's mom will scold you.

166
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:48,189
You're right.

167
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:49,819
(Don't be picky, Son.)

168
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,460
Since there were older members...

169
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,390
in the group who really liked it,

170
00:05:53,590 --> 00:05:55,766
they said, "Try it once. You'll fall in love with it." So...

171
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:56,829
And then?

172
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:58,529
- I shut my eyes and tried it, - And?

173
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:00,499
- and it was edible. - Not bad.

174
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,500
Yes, so...

175
00:06:01,501 --> 00:06:03,270
Eating cilantro for the first time in LA,

176
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:05,770
- of all places, is really funny. - That's funny.

177
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:08,370
Right. So that was how I ended up eating it this time.

178
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,640
- Great. - Gosh.

179
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:11,979
Now, let's check out Tomoya's table.

180
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,780
I'm so curious about our friend's table.

181
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:15,156
- I am a bit confident. - Sounds good.

182
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:18,320
- The drawing? - Yes, I will show you. Ta-da.

183
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:20,489
(Tomoya's table)

184
00:06:20,490 --> 00:06:21,490
He really draws well.

185
00:06:21,950 --> 00:06:23,936
Just looking at the drawing, I know what he's trying to draw.

186
00:06:23,960 --> 00:06:25,020
- Oh. - You can tell.

187
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:26,766
The food that represents you... It is that food.

188
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:29,030
- That Outback bread. - Bread?

189
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,899
That's pollock roe.

190
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,300
(Assured)

191
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,600
- Which one? - That's correct.

192
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:34,969
- The food that represents you. - Really?

193
00:06:34,970 --> 00:06:37,030
- Yes. - Pollock roe.

194
00:06:37,370 --> 00:06:40,070
- I thought it was Bushman bread. - Me too.

195
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:42,739
- It's what we have in common. - What you have in common with me?

196
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,260
Number one, Eun Ji. They are handsome.

197
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,940
No, but that was close.

198
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:48,650
- Lips. - Correct.

199
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:49,850
- Lips? - Lips.

200
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,310
Hey, mine look like blood sausages.

201
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,679
- Blood sausages? - Because they're a little thick?

202
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,690
I guess so.

203
00:06:54,750 --> 00:06:56,920
Because my lips look like pollock roe.

204
00:06:56,990 --> 00:06:57,990
That's true.

205
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,460
They are about 2.7cm.

206
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:00,806
- How many centimeters? - Did you measure?

207
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:02,489
- It's 2.7. - You measured?

208
00:07:02,490 --> 00:07:05,029
- I did. Right. - But his lips...

209
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:06,260
are nicely thick.

210
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,070
Mine just look like chicken gizzards.

211
00:07:08,270 --> 00:07:09,470
You know what I mean, right?

212
00:07:10,130 --> 00:07:11,140
That's hilarious.

213
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,800
- Thank you. - Thank you.

214
00:07:14,070 --> 00:07:16,310
Well, moving on to Yu...

215
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:17,916
I'm so curious about Yu's table from NEXZ.

216
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:20,239
- Mine is this one. - You really drew that well.

217
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,810
- Great drawing. - The quality today is really good.

218
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,720
- Totally. - Thank you.

219
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:26,080
The drawings look great today.

220
00:07:26,150 --> 00:07:27,526
The drawings really are good today.

221
00:07:27,550 --> 00:07:29,650
First, the food that represents you.

222
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:33,190
- Wait, the food that represents... - Isn't it ramen?

223
00:07:33,260 --> 00:07:34,860
- Yes, that's right. - Ramen is so...

224
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:36,159
